 *    b. By status (one search per: 'active', 'hidden', 'flagged', 'deleted') – verify search only returns posts for that status
 *    c. By author_admin_id (filter by current admin user, verify only self-authored posts returned)
 *    d. By category_id (search by each used category_id, check only posts from that category returned)
 *    e. Text search (partial title/body keywords, verify matches are as expected)
 * 4. Check pagination: use limit smaller than total (limit = 2), verify returned data and pagination meta, iterate over multiple pages if possible.
 * 5. Complex filter: status + category + text combined (ensure only posts matching all constraints are returned)
 * 6. Edge cases: 
 *    - Empty result (search with impossible filters)
 *    - Invalid category_id (well-formed but unused UUID)
 *    - Negative page index (expect graceful error handling, not internal crash)
